          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            A
            %em bicategory of relations
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%281%2C2%29-category"} (1,2)-category
            which behaves like the 2-category of internal
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/relations"} relations
            in a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/regular+category"} regular category
          %h2#definition Definition
          %p [Note: in this article, the direction of composition is diagrammatic (i.e., anti-Leibniz).]
          %p
            A
            %strong bicategory of relations
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cartesian+bicategory"} cartesian bicategory
            which is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+posetal+2-category"} locally posetal
            and moreover in which for every object
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diagonal+morphism"} diagonal
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Δ
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mi X
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta\colon X\to X\otimes X
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/codiagonal"} codiagonal
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ∇
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi X
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \nabla\colon X\otimes X\to X
            satisfy the
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Frobenius+condition"} Frobenius condition
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ∇
                  %mi Δ
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi Δ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo ∇
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \nabla\Delta = (1\otimes \Delta)(\nabla \otimes 1).
          %p
            Of course, in the locally posetal case the definition of cartesian bicategory simplifies greatly: it amounts to a symmetric monoidal
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pos"} Pos
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+category"} enriched category
            for which every object carries a commutative
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/comonoid"} comonoid
            structure, for which the structure maps
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Δ
                      %mi X
                    %mo :
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta_X: X \to X \otimes X
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi ε
                    %mi X
                  %mo :
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \varepsilon_X: X \to 1
            are
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+adjoint"} left adjoint
            1-morphisms, and for which every morphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                  %mo :
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R: X \to Y
            is a colax morphism of comonoids in the sense that the following inequalities hold:
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                  %msub
                    %mi Δ
                    %mi Y
                  %mo ≤
                  %msub
                    %mi Δ
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi R
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi R
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ,
                  %mspace{:width => "2em"}
                  %mi R
                  %msub
                    %mi ε
                    %mi Y
                  %mo ≤
                  %msub
                    %mi ε
                    %mi X
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R \Delta_Y \leq \Delta_{X \otimes X} (R \otimes R), \qquad R \varepsilon_Y \leq \varepsilon_X.
          %p
            We remark that such structure is unique when it exists (being a cartesian bicategory is a property of, as opposed to structure on, a bicategory). The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+product"} tensor product
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ⊗
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \otimes
            behaves like the ordinary product of
            = succeed "s." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/relation"} relation
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ×
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \times
            = succeed ")," do
              %em maps
          %h2#properties Properties
          %p We record a few consequences of this notion.
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              (Separability condition)
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Δ
                      %mo ∇
                      %mo =
                      %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta\nabla = 1
          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p
              In one direction, we have the 2-cell
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 1
                    %mo ≤
                    %mi Δ
                    %mo ∇
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1 \leq \Delta\nabla
              which is the unit of the adjunction
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Δ
                      %mo ⊣
                      %msub
                        %mi Δ
                        %mo *
                      %mo =
                      %mo ∇
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta \dashv \Delta_* = \nabla
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ε
                    %mo ⊣
                    %msub
                      %mi ε
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \varepsilon \dashv \varepsilon_*
              between the counit and its dual, and the unit of this adjunction is a 2-cell
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn 1
                      %mo ≤
                      %mi ε
                      %msub
                        %mi ε
                        %mo *
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1 \leq \varepsilon\varepsilon_*
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Δ
                    %mo ∇
                    %mo =
                    %mi Δ
                    %msub
                      %mi Δ
                      %mo *
                    %mo ≤
                    %mi Δ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo ×
                    %mi ε
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo ×
                    %msub
                      %mi ε
                      %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %msub
                      %mi Δ
                      %mo *
                    %mo =
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta\nabla = \Delta\Delta_* \leq \Delta (1 \times \varepsilon)(1 \times \varepsilon_*)\Delta_* = 1
            %p
              where the last equation follows from the equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Δ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo ×
                    %mi ε
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta(1 \times \varepsilon) = 1
              and its dual
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 1
                      %mo ×
                      %msub
                        %mi ε
                        %mo *
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %msub
                        %mi Δ
                        %mo *
                      %mo =
                      %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (1 \times \varepsilon_*)\Delta_* = 1
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_2 Proposition
            %p
              (Dual Frobenius condition)
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo ∇
                      %mi Δ
                      %mo =
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi Δ
                      %mo ×
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 1
                      %mo ×
                      %mo ∇
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \nabla \Delta = (\Delta \times 1)(1 \times \nabla)
          .proof
            %h6#proof_2 Proof
            %p
              The locally full subcategory whose 1-cells are
              %em maps
              (= left adjoints) has finite products, in particular a symmetry involution
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi σ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma
              for which
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Δ
                      %mi X
                    %msub
                      %mi σ
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                        %mi X
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi Δ
                      %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta_X \sigma_{X X} = \Delta_X
            %p
              Additionally, the right adjoint
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi σ
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                        %mi Y
                        %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma_{X Y *}
              is the inverse
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msubsup
                        %mi σ
                        %mrow
                          %mi X
                          %mi Y
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %mn 1
                      %mo =
                      %msub
                        %mi σ
                        %mrow
                          %mi Y
                          %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma_{X Y}^{-1} = \sigma_{Y X}
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi σ
                        %mrow
                          %mi X
                          %mi X
                      %msub
                        %mo ∇
                        %mi X
                      %mo =
                      %msub
                        %mo ∇
                        %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma_{X X} \nabla_X = \nabla_X
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mo ∇
                              %mi X
                            %msub
                              %mi Δ
                              %mi X
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi σ
                              %mrow
                                %mi X
                                %mi X
                            %msub
                              %mo ∇
                              %mi X
                            %msub
                              %mi Δ
                              %mi X
                            %msub
                              %mi σ
                              %mrow
                                %mi X
                                %mi X
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi σ
                              %mrow
                                %mi X
                                %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mn 1
                            %mo ×
                            %msub
                              %mi Δ
                              %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mo ∇
                              %mi X
                            %mo ×
                            %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %msub
                              %mi σ
                              %mrow
                                %mi X
                                %mi X
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mi Δ
                              %mi X
                            %mo ×
                            %msub
                              %mn 1
                              %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %msub
                              %mi σ
                              %mrow
                                %mi X
                                %mo ×
                                %mi X
                                %mo ,
                                %mi X
                            %msub
                              %mi σ
                              %mrow
                                %mi X
                                %mo ×
                                %mi X
                                %mo ,
                                %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mn 1
                              %mi X
                            %mo ×
                            %msub
                              %mo ∇
                              %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mi Δ
                              %mi X
                            %mo ×
                            %msub
                              %mn 1
                              %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mi σ
                              %mrow
                                %mi X
                                %mi X
                            %mo ×
                            %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mn 1
                            %mo ×
                            %msub
                              %mi σ
                              %mrow
                                %mi X
                                %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mn 1
                            %mo ×
                            %msub
                              %mo ∇
                              %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mi Δ
                              %mi X
                            %mo ×
                            %msub
                              %mn 1
                              %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mn 1
                              %mi X
                            %mo ×
                            %msub
                              %mo ∇
                              %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    \\nabla_X \Delta_X &amp; = &amp; \sigma_{X X}\nabla_X \Delta_X \sigma_{X X} \\
                    \&amp; = &amp; \sigma_{X X} (1 \times \Delta_X)(\nabla_X \times 1) \sigma_{X X} \\
                    \&amp; = &amp; (\Delta_X \times 1_X) \sigma_{X \times X, X} \sigma_{X \times X, X} (1_X \times \nabla_X) \\
                    \&amp; = &amp; (\Delta_X \times 1_X) (\sigma_{X X} \times 1) (1 \times \sigma_{X X}) (1 \times \nabla_X) \\
                    \&amp; = &amp; (\Delta_X \times 1_X)(1_X \times \nabla_X)
                    }
            %p which gives the dual equation.
          .num_theorem
            %h6#theorem Theorem
            %p In a bicategory of relations, each object is dual to itself, making the bicategory a compact closed bicategory.
          .proof
            %h6#proof_3 Proof
            %p
              Both the unit and counit of the desired adjunction
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ⊣
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \dashv X
              are given by equality predicates:
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi η
                      %mi X
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi ε
                          %mo *
                    %mi X
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mi Δ
                    %mi X
                    %mo ×
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "2em"}
                    %msub
                      %mi θ
                      %mi X
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ×
                    %mi X
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mo ∇
                    %mi X
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mi ε
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \eta_X = (1 \stackrel{\varepsilon_*}{\to} X \stackrel{\Delta}{\to} X \times X) \qquad \theta_X = (X \times X \stackrel{\nabla}{\to} X \stackrel{\varepsilon}{\to} 1)
            %p One of the triangular equations follows from the commutative diagram
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mrow
                                %mn 1
                                %mo ×
                                %msub
                                  %mi ε
                                  %mo *
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                            %mo ×
                            %mi X
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mrow
                                %mn 1
                                %mo ×
                                %mi Δ
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                            %mo ×
                            %mi X
                            %mo ×
                            %mi X
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mrow
                              %mn 1
                            %mo ↘
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                            %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                              %mo ∇
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                            %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                              %mrow
                                %mo ∇
                                %mo ×
                                %mn 1
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mi Δ
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                            %mo ×
                            %mi X
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mrow
                              %mn 1
                            %mo ↘
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                            %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                              %mrow
                                %mi ε
                                %mo ×
                                %mn 1
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    X &amp; \stackrel{1 \times \varepsilon_*}{\to} &amp; X \times X &amp; \stackrel{1 \times \Delta}{\to} &amp; X \times X \times X \\
                    \&amp; {}_1\searrow &amp; \downarrow \mathrlap{\nabla} &amp; &amp; \downarrow \mathrlap{\nabla \times 1} \\
                    \&amp; &amp; X &amp; \overset{\Delta}{\to} &amp; X \times X \\
                    \&amp; &amp;  &amp; {}_{1}\searrow &amp; \downarrow \mathrlap{\varepsilon \times 1} \\
                    \&amp; &amp; &amp; &amp; X
                    }
            %p where the square expresses a Frobenius equation. The other triangular equation uses the dual Frobenius equation.
          %p
            The compact closure allows us to define the opposite of a relation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                  %mo :
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R: X \to Y
            as the 1-morphism mate:
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi R
                    %mi op
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Y
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mn 1
                        %mi Y
                      %mo ×
                      %msub
                        %mi η
                        %mi X
                  %mi Y
                  %mo ×
                  %mi X
                  %mo ×
                  %mi X
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mn 1
                        %mi Y
                      %mo ×
                      %mi R
                      %mo ×
                      %msub
                        %mn 1
                        %mi X
                  %mi Y
                  %mo ×
                  %mi Y
                  %mo ×
                  %mi X
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi θ
                        %mi Y
                      %mo ×
                      %msub
                        %mn 1
                        %mi X
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R^{op} = (Y \stackrel{1_Y \times \eta_X}{\to} Y \times X \times X \stackrel{1_Y \times R \times 1_X}{\to} Y \times Y \times X \stackrel{\theta_Y \times 1_X}{\to} X)
          %p
            In this way, a bicategory of relations becomes a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dagger-compact+category"} †-compact
            = succeed "-enriched" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Pos
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Pos
          %p
            Recall (again) that a
            %strong map
            in the bicategory of relations is the same as a 1-cell that has a right adjoint.
          #strict.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_3 Proposition
            %p
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \colon X \to Y
              is a map, then
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              is a strict morphism of comonoids.
          .proof
